window.docContents[43].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___25-Continued-Fractions/#chapter-4-section-25":{"contents":"Source: NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, §4.25.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions","header":"4.25. §4.25 Continued Fractions","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___25-Continued-Fractions/#chapter-4-section-25"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___21-Software/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___21-Software--___6___21-Software--Complex-arguments":{"contents":"For\nE_{1}(z),\\ \\operatorname{Si}(z),\\ \\operatorname{Ci}(z),\\ \\operatorname{Shi}(z),\\ \\operatorname{Chi}(z),\\qquad z\\in\\mathbb{C}$$\nthe DLMF lists Amos (1990), again identified as Fortran. The complex-argument\nentry is separate from the real-argument list because it covers a different\ndomain and a different implementation reference.\n\n\n\nThe DLMF Software Cross Index provides the corresponding navigation for both\nthe real and complex entries. No numbered equation, table, or figure occurs in\n§6.21; the page's substantive content is the software bibliography and its\ndomain split.\n\nend LMLFManual.Chapter6\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.21 Software\u0009§6.21 Software","header":"Complex arguments","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___21-Software/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___21-Software--___6___21-Software--Complex-arguments"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___5-Further-Interrelations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___5-Further-Interrelations--___6___5-Further-Interrelations":{"contents":"The first four formulas describe genuine one-sided limits of the canonical\nprincipal E₁ branch on its negative-real cut and their principal-value\naverage, then identify the canonical hyperbolic sine and cosine integrals.\nThey are stated for positive real x; the sign σ=±1 records the\nupper/lower limiting side and is not collapsed into a totalized value at the\ncut.  E5–E6 use the canonical §6.2 functions directly at the rotated\narguments ±iz, with |arg z| < π/2 and z ≠ 0.  E7 uses the canonical\n§6.2 auxiliary functions and principal E₁ map, with both signs explicit.\nThe named e1CutBoundary x σ records the corresponding canonical limit\nvalue, so E1 and E2 do not quantify arbitrary side-limit outputs.\n\nE_{1}(-x\\pm i0)=-\\operatorname{Ei}(x)\\mp i\\pi,\\quad x>0$$\n\n\\operatorname{Ei}(x)=-\\tfrac12(E_{1}(-x+i0)+E_{1}(-x-i0)),\\quad x>0$$\n\n\\tfrac12(\\operatorname{Ei}(x)+E_{1}(x))=\\operatorname{Shi}(x)=-i\\operatorname{Si}(ix),\\quad x>0$$\n\n\\tfrac12(\\operatorname{Ei}(x)-E_{1}(x))=\\operatorname{Chi}(x)=\\operatorname{Ci}(ix)-\\tfrac12\\pi i,\\quad x>0$$\n\n\\operatorname{Si}(z)=\\tfrac12i(E_{1}(-iz)-E_{1}(iz))+\\tfrac12\\pi$$\n\n\\operatorname{Ci}(z)=-\\tfrac12(E_{1}(iz)+E_{1}(-iz))$$\n\ng(z)\\pm if(z)=E_{1}(\\mp iz)e^{\\mp iz}$$\n\nThe DLMF source cites Olver (1997b),\np. 41, for E1 and\nE2, and p. 42 for\nE5 and E6.\nIt records that E3 and E4 follow from\n6.6.E1,\n6.6.E2,\n6.6.E5, and\n6.6.E6, while E7 follows from\n6.2.E10,\n6.2.E17,\n6.2.E18,\nE5, and\nE6.\nThese are source dependencies, not additional numbered formulas.\n\nThe first four interrelations use positive real x; the two cut values retain\nthe upper and lower signs separately, while E3 and E4 use the canonical\npositive-real Ei, E₁, Shi, and Chi values.\n\nFor E5, E6, and E7 the source condition is |ph z| < π/2, represented here by\n‖Complex.arg z‖ < π/2.  E7 also retains the honest Lean endpoint condition\nz ≠ 0, because the formal arg map is totalized at zero; this prevents the\ncanonical rotated E₁ values from being read at the singular endpoint.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.5 Further Interrelations","header":"§6.5 Further Interrelations","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___5-Further-Interrelations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___5-Further-Interrelations--___6___5-Further-Interrelations"},"/Incomplete-Gamma-and-Related-Functions/Chapter-contents/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Incomplete-Gamma-and-Related-Functions--Chapter-contents":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Incomplete Gamma and Related Functions","header":"Chapter contents","id":"/Incomplete-Gamma-and-Related-Functions/Chapter-contents/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Incomplete-Gamma-and-Related-Functions--Chapter-contents"}});